WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.476
Timing matters because attention and energy fluctuate.

00:00:02.476 --> 00:00:07.229
When practical, schedule difficult learning when alertness is higher for the learner or group.

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:10.623
This does not mean everyone has the same ideal schedule.

00:00:10.623 --> 00:00:15.376
It means training plans should respect the fact that demanding material requires mental resources,

00:00:15.376 --> 00:00:18.431
and those resources are not constant throughout the day.

00:00:18.431 --> 00:00:21.486
Distributed practice is often stronger than one long session.

00:00:21.486 --> 00:00:25.559
Spacing learning across time gives learners multiple chances to retrieve, review, sleep,

00:00:25.559 --> 00:00:26.238
and return.

00:00:26.238 --> 00:00:31.670
Evening review can be useful at a general level when it is brief and not disruptive.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:36.083
Morning review can help learners test what remains available after time has passed.

00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:38.798
The key is repeated retrieval, not endless rereading.

00:00:38.798 --> 00:00:41.514
Breaks and recovery days matter for demanding learning.

00:00:41.514 --> 00:00:45.927
A full day of intense practice may produce diminishing returns if attention collapses.

00:00:45.927 --> 00:00:47.624
Short breaks can restore focus.

00:00:47.624 --> 00:00:51.358
Recovery days can help when learning is emotionally or cognitively demanding.

00:00:51.358 --> 00:00:53.735
The goal is not to avoid effort.

00:00:53.735 --> 00:00:57.469
The goal is to preserve enough quality that practice remains useful.

00:00:57.469 --> 00:00:59.845
Avoid extreme routines and idealized productivity advice.

00:00:59.845 --> 00:01:03.239
Real learners have jobs, caregiving, commutes, health needs, and interruptions.

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:07.992
A sustainable schedule is better than a perfect schedule that collapses after three days.

00:01:07.992 --> 00:01:10.708
Align practice with real life: choose repeatable blocks,

00:01:10.708 --> 00:01:15.460
protect the hardest work when possible, and make it easy to restart after interruptions.
